    ["#283747","A shower of black floaters and a dark curtain across vision","Retinal detachment",["Migraine","Normal floaters","Cataract"],"Same-day eye emergency. Flashes plus new floaters need a retina check.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Retinal%20detachment"],
    ["#F8F9F9","White patches inside the mouth that wipe off, leaving red skin","Oral thrush",["Leukoplakia","Lichen planus","Oral hairy leukoplakia"],"Candida. Common with inhaled steroids (rinse after use), antibiotics and dentures.","/oral-thrush-babies/"],
    ["#FDFEFE","A white patch on the side of the tongue that won’t wipe off","Leukoplakia",["Oral thrush","Lichen planus","Oral hairy leukoplakia"],"Can be pre-cancerous, especially in smokers. Needs a biopsy if it persists over 2 weeks.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Leukoplakia"],
    ["#FFFFFF","A white pupil instead of red eye in a baby’s flash photo","Retinoblastoma",["Strabismus","Conjunctivitis","Normal finding"],"Retinoblastoma until proven otherwise. Could also be cataract. Any white pupil reflex in a child needs an urgent eye review.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Retinoblastoma"],
    ["#F4F6F6","Paired white bands across all the fingernails that don’t grow out","Muehrcke’s lines",["Mees’ lines","Beau’s lines","Leukonychia"],"Swollen nail bed from low albumin, e.g. nephrotic syndrome. Lines in the nail itself (Mees’) grow out instead.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Muehrckes%20lines"],
    ["#ECF0F1","Chalky white lumps on the ear rims and finger joints","Gout tophi",["Rheumatoid nodules","Calcinosis","Heberden’s nodes"],"Urate deposits after years of high uric acid. They shrink with urate-lowering treatment.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Gout%20tophi"],
    ["#FBFCFC","Tiny white spots inside the cheek, a day or two before a rash","Measles",["Thrush","Hand, foot and mouth","Chickenpox"],"Like grains of salt on a red background. Measles is highly contagious; vaccination prevents it.","/measles/"],
    ["#F2F3F4","Milky white blood serum in the lab tube","Very high triglycerides",["Haemolysed sample","High bilirubin","Paraproteinaemia"],"Lipaemic serum. Levels over 10 mmol/L risk pancreatitis.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Very%20high%20triglycerides"],
    ["#EAEDED","Pale, milky nails with a narrow pink band at the tips","Terry’s nails",["Lindsay’s nails","Muehrcke’s lines","Fungal nail infection"],"Seen in cirrhosis, heart failure and kidney disease. Also with ageing.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Terrys%20nails"],
    ["#FDFEFE","Symmetrical patches of skin losing all colour","Vitiligo",["Fungal infection","Burns","Albinism"],"Autoimmune loss of pigment cells. Check thyroid. Treatments include creams and light therapy.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Vitiligo"],
    ["#F7F9F9","Milky white urine in someone who lived in the tropics","Chyluria",["Phosphaturia","Pyuria from a UTI","Proteinuria"],"Often from lymphatic filariasis. Lymph leaks into the urinary tract. Filariasis is the leading cause worldwide.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Chyluria"],
    ["#F0F3F4","Fingers going white and numb after 20 years on a jackhammer","Hand-arm vibration syndrome",["Raynaud’s from scleroderma","Carpal tunnel","Frostbite"],"An occupational disease. Limit exposure time and keep hands warm.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Hand-arm%20vibration%20syndrome"],
    ["#95A5A6","A grey, floppy newborn on an antibiotic","Chloramphenicol toxicity",["Sepsis","Hypothermia","Heart defect"],"Newborns can’t break down chloramphenicol, so it builds up and causes collapse.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Chloramphenicol%20toxicity"],
    ["#AAB7B8","A grey-white membrane over the tonsils that bleeds when scraped, and a ‘bull neck’","Diphtheria",["Tonsillitis","Glandular fever","Thrush"],"A toxin-producing bacterium. Vaccination nearly eliminated it; it returns when coverage drops.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Diphtheria"],
    ["#BDC3C7","A grey-white ring around the edge of the cornea in an older person","Arcus senilis",["Kayser–Fleischer ring","Corneal ulcer","Pinguecula"],"Normal with age. In people under 50, check cholesterol.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Arcus%20senilis"],
    ["#B2BABB","Thin grey discharge with a fishy smell","Bacterial vaginosis",["Thrush","Gonorrhoea","Normal discharge"],"An overgrowth of anaerobic bacteria; not an STI. Treated with metronidazole.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Bacterial%20vaginosis"],
    ["#C0C0C0","Silvery scales on red plaques on the elbows and knees","Psoriasis",["Eczema","Ringworm","Dermatitis"],"An immune skin disease, linked to arthritis and heart disease. Many effective treatments now exist.","/psoriasis/"],
    ["#A6ACAF","Silver, aluminium-paint-coloured stools","Ampullary cancer",["Barium meal","Bismuth","Pancreatic cancer"],"Bleeding plus a blocked bile duct. Pale stools from blocked bile mixed with blood make a silver colour. Rare, and a classic exam clue.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Ampullary%20cancer"],
    ["#909497","Blue-grey skin after years of gold injections for arthritis","Chrysiasis",["Argyria","Cyanosis","Haemochromatosis"],"Gold deposits. Gold builds up in sun-exposed skin. Gold treatment is now rarely used.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Chrysiasis"],
    ["#E74C3C","A ringed, red, scaly patch with a clearer centre, spreading outwards","Tinea corporis",["Eczema","Psoriasis","Lyme disease"],"Ringworm. A fungus, not a worm. Antifungal cream for 2 weeks; steroid creams make it worse.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Tinea%20corporis"],
    ["#FF6F61","Red, cracked corners of the mouth","Angular cheilitis",["Cold sore","Impetigo","Lip cancer"],"Often thrush or staph in skin folds, or low iron or B vitamins, or ill-fitting dentures.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Angular%20cheilitis"],
    ["#C39BD3","Blue-purple lips and nails in someone with very low oxygen levels","Cyanosis",["Methaemoglobinaemia","Argyria","Raynaud’s phenomenon"],"Over about 50 g/L of deoxygenated haemoglobin makes skin and nails blue. Harder to see with anaemia or darker skin.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Cyanosis"],
    ["#F9E79F","Yellow-tinged eyes and skin after starting a new antibiotic","Drug-induced cholestasis",["Hepatitis A","Gilbert syndrome","Carotenaemia"],"E.g. amoxicillin-clavulanate. Amoxicillin-clavulanate is one of the commonest causes of drug liver injury, sometimes weeks after the course ends.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Drug-induced%20cholestasis"],
    ["#1ABC9C","Teal-blue discolouration of the skin after a sentinel node biopsy","Patent blue dye",["Cyanosis","Bruising","Argyria"],"Isosulfan. The dye used to find lymph nodes can stain skin for months and briefly turn urine blue-green.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Patent%20blue%20dye"],
    ["#A04000","Rust-coloured sputum with fever and pleuritic pain","Pneumococcal pneumonia",["Tuberculosis","Lung cancer","Bronchitis"],"Classic of lobar pneumonia from Streptococcus pneumoniae. Vaccines help prevent it.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pneumococcal%20pneumonia"],
    ["#C0392B","Red-currant-jelly sputum in an older person who drinks heavily","Klebsiella pneumonia",["Tuberculosis","Pulmonary embolism","Asthma"],"Thick, bloody sputum. Often in alcohol use disorder or diabetes.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Klebsiella%20pneumonia"],
    ["#D7BDE2","Lilac, thickened patches on the skin with a purple edge","Morphoea",["Lichen sclerosus","Necrobiosis lipoidica","Granuloma annulare"],"Localised scleroderma. Skin-only scleroderma. The lilac ring marks active inflammation.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Morphoea"],
    ["#FAD02E","Yellow-white raised spots on the face of a newborn","Milia",["Neonatal acne","Sebaceous hyperplasia","Erythema toxicum"],"Tiny keratin cysts. Harmless and gone within weeks. Don’t squeeze.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Milia"],
    ["#FFB6C1","A pink-orange stain in a newborn’s nappy","Urate crystals",["Blood in the urine","Pseudomenses","Bilirubin in the urine"],"Brick dust. Common in the first days before feeding is established. If persistent, check feeding and hydration.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Urate%20crystals"],
    ["#4A235A","Dark bruising around both eyes a day after a head injury","Basal skull fracture",["Orbital fracture","Allergic shiners","Nasal fracture"],"Raccoon eyes. Blood tracks from the skull base into the eye sockets. Ask about clear fluid from the nose or ears. CT needed.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Basal%20skull%20fracture"],
    ["#D4AC0D","Thick, crumbly, yellow-brown toenails","Onychomycosis",["Psoriatic nails","Yellow nail syndrome","Onychogryphosis"],"Onychomycosis. Confirm with clippings before months of treatment: psoriasis can look identical.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Onychomycosis"],
    ["#7D3C98","Purple, swollen gums that bleed, and corkscrew-shaped hairs","Scurvy",["Gum disease","Leukaemia","Lichen planus"],"Still seen with very restricted diets. Vitamin C is needed to make collagen. Sailors once carried limes for this reason.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Scurvy"],
    ["#1B2631","A blue-black patch under a big toenail after a long run","Subungual haematoma",["Melanoma","Fungal nail","Splinter haemorrhage"],"Blood under the nail. It grows out with the nail; a streak that doesn’t needs a melanoma check.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Subungual%20haematoma"],
    ["#F4D03F","Small yellow spots at the back of the eye in an older person","Drusen",["Cataract","Diabetic retinopathy","Glaucoma"],"Early macular degeneration. Deposits under the retina. Stop smoking; check central vision with an Amsler grid.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Drusen"],
    ["#E74C3C","Cherry-red skin, headache and confusion in a family sharing a house with a faulty heater","Carbon monoxide poisoning",["Cyanide poisoning","Influenza","Methaemoglobinaemia"],"Cherry-red colour is a late and unreliable sign. Pulse oximeters read falsely normal; check a blood gas with CO-oximetry.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Carbon%20monoxide%20poisoning"],
    ["#CB4335","Hot, red, swollen shin with a sharp, raised edge and a fever","Erysipelas",["Gout","Deep vein thrombosis","Eczema"],"A superficial strep infection of the skin. The crisp edge sets it apart from deeper cellulitis.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Erysipelas"],
    ["#E35D5B","Bright red ‘slapped’ cheeks, then a lacy rash on the arms in a child who feels well","Parvovirus B19",["Scarlet fever","Measles","Rubella"],"Fifth disease. Usually mild, but tell pregnant contacts: it can affect the unborn baby.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Parvovirus%20B19"],
    ["#EC7063","Red target-shaped spots on the palms a week after a cold sore","Erythema multiforme",["Hand, foot and mouth disease","Urticaria","Fixed drug eruption"],"Usually triggered by herpes simplex. Targets have three rings. Settles by itself in a few weeks.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Erythema%20multiforme"],
    ["#F1948A","Small red bumps and scale around the mouth and nose, sparing a thin rim at the lip edge","Perioral dermatitis",["Rosacea","Seborrhoeic dermatitis","Impetigo"],"Often follows steroid creams on the face. Stop the steroid; it may flare first.","/perioral-dermatitis/"],
    ["#E6564B","Red cheeks and nose with flushing and pimples, but no blackheads","Rosacea",["Acne vulgaris","Lupus","Seborrhoeic dermatitis"],"No blackheads (comedones) sets it apart from acne. Triggers include heat, alcohol and spicy food.","/rosacea/"],
    ["#FF6F61","Itchy red welts that move around, each lasting less than a day","Urticaria",["Erythema multiforme","Urticarial vasculitis","Insect bites"],"Hives. Individual welts come and go within 24 hours. Antihistamines are first line.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Urticaria"],
    ["#C0392B","Red flushed face, headache and diarrhoea within an hour of eating tuna steak","Scombroid poisoning",["Seafood allergy","Food poisoning (salmonella)","Ciguatera"],"Histamine builds up in badly stored fish. Antihistamines work; it isn’t an allergy.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Scombroid%20poisoning"],
    ["#922B21","Red, blistering rash and sore mouth and eyes two weeks after starting lamotrigine","Stevens–Johnson syndrome",["Erythema multiforme","Toxic shock syndrome","DRESS syndrome"],"A skin emergency. Stop the drug and get to hospital; eye checks are urgent.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Stevens%E2%80%93Johnson%20syndrome"],
    ["#B03A2E","Red-purple spots that don’t fade under a glass, in a feverish, drowsy child","Meningococcal sepsis",["Henoch–Schönlein purpura","Viral rash","Immune thrombocytopenia"],"Non-blanching rash plus fever needs IV antibiotics now, before tests.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Meningococcal%20sepsis"],
    ["#F5B7B1","A little blood in the nappy of a 5-day-old baby girl","Pseudomenses",["Urinary tract infection","Bowel bleeding","Injury"],"Pseudomenses. Mum’s hormones drop after birth. Harmless and settles in a few days.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pseudomenses"],
    ["#CB4335","Coral-red glow under a Wood’s lamp in a brown, scaly groin rash","Erythrasma",["Tinea cruris","Psoriasis","Candida"],"A Corynebacterium infection. Bacteria make porphyrins that glow coral red.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Erythrasma"],
    ["#E74C3C","Red, swollen, painful ear that spares the earlobe, on both sides","Relapsing polychondritis",["Ear infection","Cellulitis","Gout"],"Cartilage is inflamed, and the lobe has none. Can also affect the nose, airway and eyes.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Relapsing%20polychondritis"],
    ["#E67E22","Oily orange spotting on underwear after starting a weight-loss tablet","Orlistat",["Bowel infection","Haemorrhoids","Bile acid diarrhoea"],"Orlistat blocks fat absorption; the undigested fat leaks out. Less fat in the diet means fewer accidents.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Orlistat"],
    ["#D35400","Orange-brown spots like cayenne pepper in patches on both shins","Pigmented purpuric dermatosis",["Vasculitis","Low platelets","Bruising"],"Schamberg disease. Leaky capillaries leave iron behind. Harmless, though it can last years.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pigmented%20purpuric%20dermatosis"],
    ["#E8743B","Orange-red skin of the palms with thick scale and ‘islands’ of normal skin","Pityriasis rubra pilaris",["Psoriasis","Eczema","Carotenaemia"],"A rare scaly skin condition. The islands of sparing are the clue.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pityriasis%20rubra%20pilaris"],
    ["#EB984E","Orange-tan skin colour that won’t fade, in someone drinking litres of tomato juice","Lycopenaemia",["Jaundice","Addison’s disease","Carotenaemia"],"Lycopene from tomatoes stains the skin, like carotene from carrots. Eyes stay white.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Lycopenaemia"],
    ["#F39C12","Yellow-orange shiny plaques on the shins of a woman with diabetes","Necrobiosis lipoidica",["Shin bruising","Psoriasis","Pretibial myxoedema"],"Often painless and can ulcerate. Linked with diabetes but can occur without it.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Necrobiosis%20lipoidica"],
    ["#A04000","Red-brown skin and orange tears in a man treated for leprosy","Clofazimine",["Rifampicin","Jaundice","Addison’s disease"],"Clofazimine deposits in the skin. It fades slowly after stopping.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Clofazimine"],
    ["#F4D03F","Neon-yellow urine after a multivitamin","Riboflavin",["Rifampicin","Phenazopyridine","Jaundice"],"Riboflavin fluoresces yellow. Harmless.","/riboflavin/"],
    ["#F7DC6F","Thick yellow greasy scale on a baby’s scalp","Cradle cap",["Eczema","Ringworm","Psoriasis"],"Infant seborrhoeic dermatitis. Harmless. Soften with oil and brush gently. Usually gone by 12 months.","/cradle-cap/"],
    ["#F1C40F","A bulging, yellow eardrum in a feverish toddler pulling at the ear","Acute otitis media",["Earwax","Swimmer’s ear","Glue ear"],"A bulging drum is the most reliable sign. Many settle without antibiotics.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Acute%20otitis%20media"],
    ["#F9E79F","Painful round yellow-grey sore inside the lip with a red halo","Aphthous ulcer",["Oral cancer","Herpes","Thrush"],"Common and recurrent. One lasting over 3 weeks needs checking.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Aphthous%20ulcer"],
    ["#D4AC0D","Yellow skin in a newborn within the first 24 hours of life","Pathological jaundice",["Normal newborn jaundice","Breast milk jaundice","Gilbert syndrome"],"Often blood group haemolysis. Jaundice in the first day is never normal. Check bilirubin and blood group urgently.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pathological%20jaundice"],
    ["#F4D03F","Yellow-orange streaks in the creases of the palms","Palmar xanthomas",["Carotenaemia","Jaundice","Calluses"],"Type III dyslipidaemia. A clue to dysbetalipoproteinaemia, a rare inherited lipid disorder with high heart risk.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Palmar%20xanthomas"],
    ["#F7DC6F","A yellowish raised bump on the white of the eye beside the cornea","Pinguecula",["Melanoma of the eye","Conjunctivitis","Arcus senilis"],"Sun and wind damage. Harmless; lubricating drops help irritation.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pinguecula"],
    ["#F5B041","Thick yellow discharge from the penis and burning when weeing","Gonorrhoea",["Chlamydia only","Urinary tract infection","Thrush"],"Test with a swab and urine PCR. Treat with ceftriaxone and notify partners.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Gonorrhoea"],
    ["#C9A227","Frothy yellow-green, fishy discharge with a ‘strawberry’ cervix","Trichomoniasis",["Bacterial vaginosis","Thrush","Gonorrhoea"],"A parasite. Treat with metronidazole, and treat partners too.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Trichomoniasis"],
    ["#F9E79F","Yellow fluid in the CSF 12 hours after a thunderclap headache","Subarachnoid haemorrhage",["Meningitis","Traumatic tap","Normal CSF"],"Subarachnoid haemorrhage. Red cells break down to bilirubin, which takes hours. That’s why the LP is timed 12 hours after onset.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Subarachnoid%20haemorrhage"],
    ["#27AE60","Green, sticky ‘tar’ in a newborn’s first nappies","Meconium",["Bilious vomit","Melaena","Changing stools"],"Normal first poo. No meconium by 48 hours raises concern for Hirschsprung disease or cystic fibrosis.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Meconium"],
    ["#2E8B57","Green amniotic fluid when the waters break at 41 weeks","Meconium-stained liquor",["Chorioamnionitis","Placental abruption","Bloody show"],"Common after term. Thick meconium can signal distress; the baby is watched closely.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Meconium-stained%20liquor"],
    ["#52BE80","A shin blotch, purple last week, now green and yellow","Healing bruise",["Bleeding disorder","Cellulitis","Erythema nodosum"],"Haemoglobin breaks down to green biliverdin, then yellow bilirubin. You can’t reliably date a bruise by colour.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Healing%20bruise"],
    ["#1ABC9C","Blue-green glow under a Wood’s lamp in a child’s scaly scalp patch","Tinea capitis",["Psoriasis","Alopecia areata","Cradle cap"],"Microsporum. Needs oral antifungals; creams don’t reach the hair roots. The common Trichophyton type doesn’t glow.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Tinea%20capitis"],
    ["#16A085","A bright green-yellow streak on the eye after fluorescein drops, after a twig flicked it","Corneal abrasion",["Glaucoma","Conjunctivitis","Retinal detachment"],"Fluorescein glows where the surface is missing. Most heal within 1 to 2 days.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Corneal%20abrasion"],
    ["#239B56","Green-black vomit in an adult with a swollen, tight abdomen","Bowel obstruction",["Gastroenteritis","Pancreatitis","Gastric outlet obstruction"],"Bilious vomiting means the blockage is below the bile duct. Needs urgent imaging.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Bowel%20obstruction"],
    ["#2E86DE","Toddler cries hard when told no, goes silent, turns blue and floppy for seconds, then recovers","Breath-holding spell",["Seizure","Heart problem","Choking"],"Frightening but harmless. Check for iron deficiency, which makes them more common.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Breath-holding%20spell"],
    ["#5DADE2","Blue hands and feet in a newborn, pink lips and body","Acrocyanosis",["Heart disease","Cold injury","Sepsis"],"Normal in the first days. Blue lips or tongue (central cyanosis) is the worry.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Acrocyanosis"],
    ["#2E86C1","Blue-green urine after surgery to find a sentinel lymph node","Methylene blue",["Pseudomonas","Propofol","Kidney failure"],"Dyes are passed in the urine. Harmless, but methylene blue can interact with serotonin medicines.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Methylene%20blue"],
    ["#3498DB","Bluish cervix at 8 weeks","Early pregnancy",["Cervical cancer","Cervicitis","Cervical ectropion"],"Chadwick’s sign. Extra blood flow in pregnancy. A pregnancy test is more reliable.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Early%20pregnancy"],
    ["#1F618D","Bluish bruising around the belly button in a man with severe upper abdominal pain","Retroperitoneal bleeding",["Hernia","Bruise from a fall","Umbilical infection"],"Cullen’s sign. Seen in severe pancreatitis or a ruptured ectopic pregnancy. A late sign.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Retroperitoneal%20bleeding"],
    ["#2874A6","Blue-purple ‘blueberry muffin’ spots in a newborn","Congenital infection",["Bruising from birth","Mongolian spots","Haemangioma"],"E.g. CMV or rubella. Blood is being made in the skin. Also seen in some cancers; needs urgent assessment.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Congenital%20infection"],
    ["#5499C7","Blue lips and a pulse oximeter reading of 82% at a ski resort in the Himalayas","High-altitude hypoxia",["High-altitude pulmonary oedema","Methaemoglobinaemia","Hypothermia"],"Air pressure falls with height. Go down if there’s breathlessness at rest or confusion.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=High-altitude%20hypoxia"],
    ["#8E44AD","Purple raised spots on the legs and buttocks, tummy pain and sore knees in a child","IgA vasculitis",["Meningococcal sepsis","Bruising","Leukaemia"],"Henoch–Schönlein purpura. Usually settles, but check urine and blood pressure for kidney involvement for 6 months.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=IgA%20vasculitis"],
    ["#7D3C98","A swollen, painful, purple-blue leg after a big DVT","Phlegmasia cerulea dolens",["Cellulitis","Simple DVT","Lymphoedema"],"Blocked veins cut off arterial flow. A limb emergency: urgent clot treatment.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Phlegmasia%20cerulea%20dolens"],
    ["#9B59B6","Violet, shiny plaques over the nose and cheeks","Lupus pernio",["Rosacea","Lupus","Frostbite"],"A skin form of sarcoidosis, often with lung and upper airway involvement.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Lupus%20pernio"],
    ["#A569BD","Itchy purple-red bumps on the toes after cold, damp weather","Chilblains",["Frostbite","Raynaud’s","Gout"],"Pernio. An abnormal reaction of small vessels to cold. Keep warm; avoid rapid rewarming.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Chilblains"],
    ["#5B2C6F","Purple, swollen skin with blisters and pain far worse than it looks","Necrotising fasciitis",["Cellulitis","Gas gangrene","Pyoderma gangrenosum"],"A surgical emergency. Pain out of proportion is the key early clue.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Necrotising%20fasciitis"],
    ["#FFB6C1","Pink, gritty, watery eyes with a tender lump in front of the ear","Viral conjunctivitis",["Bacterial conjunctivitis","Allergic conjunctivitis","Herpes simplex keratitis"],"Adenovirus. Very contagious. Antibiotics don’t help. Wash hands and don’t share towels.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Viral%20conjunctivitis"],
    ["#F1948A","Bright pink skin, confusion and a very high lactate, with carboxyhaemoglobin only 4%, after a house fire","Cyanide poisoning",["Carbon monoxide poisoning","Methaemoglobinaemia","Smoke inhalation alone"],"Burning plastics release cyanide. Very high lactate is a clue; hydroxocobalamin is the antidote.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Cyanide%20poisoning"],
    ["#FADBD8","Pink, blotchy rash on the trunk just as three days of high fever break, in a baby","Roseola",["Measles","Antibiotic allergy","Rubella"],"HHV-6. The rash appears as the fever goes. Harmless; febrile seizures can happen during the fever.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Roseola"],
    ["#F5B7B1","A pink, pearly lump with a rolled edge and tiny surface vessels on the nose","Basal cell carcinoma",["Squamous cell carcinoma","Amelanotic melanoma","Sebaceous hyperplasia"],"The most common skin cancer in Australia. Rarely spreads, but grows locally; remove it.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Basal%20cell%20carcinoma"],
    ["#EC7063","A pink, tender lump in a baby’s groin that won’t push back in","Incarcerated inguinal hernia",["Swollen lymph node","Hydrocele","Undescended testis"],"Needs urgent surgical review. Gentle reduction is often tried first.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Incarcerated%20inguinal%20hernia"],
    ["#6E4B3A","Rusty brown discolouration of the lower legs above the ankles, with varicose veins","Venous disease",["Bruising","Addison’s disease","Melanoma"],"Iron from leaked red cells stains the skin. A sign of chronic venous insufficiency; compression helps.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Venous%20disease"],
    ["#7B4B2A","Brown, warty, ‘stuck-on’ spots on the back of an older person","Seborrhoeic keratoses",["Melanoma","Actinic keratoses","Pigmented basal cell carcinoma"],"Harmless. One that looks different from the rest (‘ugly duckling’) needs checking.","/seborrhoeic-keratosis/"],
    ["#A0522D","A brown line down the middle of the belly in pregnancy","Linea nigra",["Addison’s disease","Bruising","Melanoma"],"Pregnancy hormones darken skin. It fades after birth.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Linea%20nigra"],
    ["#4E342E","A dark, carpet-like coating on the top of the tongue after a course of antibiotics","Black hairy tongue",["Oral thrush","Melanoma","Iron tablets"],"Overgrown tongue papillae trap pigment. Brushing the tongue fixes it.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Black%20hairy%20tongue"],
    ["#B5651D","Brown flecks and white spots on children’s teeth in an area with mineral-rich bore water","Dental fluorosis",["Tooth decay","Tetracycline staining","Iron syrup staining"],"Too much fluoride while teeth are forming. Cosmetic only.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Dental%20fluorosis"],
    ["#6D4C41","Brown-black dots in a painful sole callus after paring it back","Plantar wart",["Corn","Talon noir","Melanoma"],"The dots are tiny clotted capillaries. Corns don’t have them.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Plantar%20wart"],
    ["#1C1C1C","Black crust on the palate and a swollen face in a person with poorly controlled diabetes","Mucormycosis",["Melanoma","Dental abscess","Sinusitis only"],"An aggressive fungal infection. Needs surgery and amphotericin urgently.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Mucormycosis"],
    ["#212121","Black sputum in a retired coal miner","Pneumoconiosis",["Lung cancer","Tuberculosis","Aspergilloma"],"Melanoptysis. Breakdown of coal dust nodules. Silica exposure also raises TB and lung cancer risk.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pneumoconiosis"],
    ["#17202A","Painless black dots on the heel of a basketball player","Talon noir",["Acral melanoma","Plantar wart","Subungual haematoma"],"Black heel. Tiny bleeds from shear forces. Paring it away removes the colour; melanoma won’t pare off.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Talon%20noir"],
    ["#2C3E50","Grey-blue patches on the shins and hard palate after years of antimalarial tablets","Hydroxychloroquine pigmentation",["Addison’s disease","Bruising","Haemochromatosis"],"Usually on the shins and face. Also needs regular eye checks for retinal toxicity.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Hydroxychloroquine%20pigmentation"],
    ["#FDFEFE","White patches on swollen tonsils, a big spleen and tiredness in a teenager","Glandular fever",["Strep throat","Tonsillar cancer","Thrush"],"EBV. Avoid contact sport for at least 3 weeks: the spleen can rupture. Amoxicillin causes a rash.","/glandular-fever/"],
    ["#F8F9F9","Small white spots on the fingernails that grow out","Leukonychia",["Calcium deficiency","Zinc deficiency","Fungal infection"],"Minor nail injury. Usually from small knocks to the nail base, not low calcium.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Leukonychia"],
    ["#FFFFFF","Thick white ‘cottage cheese’ discharge and itch","Vaginal thrush",["Bacterial vaginosis","Trichomoniasis","Gonorrhoea"],"Candidiasis. Common after antibiotics. Bacterial vaginosis is thin and fishy instead.","/thrush/"],
    ["#F4F6F6","Milky white fluid in a chest drain after heart surgery","Chylothorax",["Empyema","Haemothorax","Pseudochylothorax"],"Lymph leaking from a damaged thoracic duct. High triglycerides in the fluid confirm it.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Chylothorax"],
    ["#ECF0F1","White, ridged patches on the sides of the tongue that won’t scrape off, in a person with HIV","Oral hairy leukoplakia",["Oral thrush","Lichen planus","Geographic tongue"],"EBV. Harmless itself, but a sign of low immunity.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Oral%20hairy%20leukoplakia"],
    ["#F2F3F4","Pale, slightly scaly patches on a child’s cheeks after summer","Pityriasis alba",["Vitiligo","Tinea","Pityriasis versicolor"],"A mild form of eczema. Moisturiser and sunscreen help; it fades.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pityriasis%20alba"],
    ["#FBFCFC","Pale patches on the back that don’t tan after a beach holiday, with fine scale","Pityriasis versicolor",["Vitiligo","Pityriasis alba","Ringworm"],"A yeast (Malassezia) overgrowth. Antifungal shampoo on the skin treats it; colour returns slowly.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pityriasis%20versicolor"],
    ["#EAEDED","White, powdery frost on the skin of a person with untreated kidney failure","Uraemic frost",["Calciphylaxis","Pityriasis versicolor","Ichthyosis"],"Urea crystallises from sweat. Very rare now that dialysis is available.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Uraemic%20frost"],
    ["#F0F3F4","Hard white chalky lumps in the fingertips with tight, shiny skin","Calcinosis",["Gout tophi","Heberden’s nodes","Rheumatoid nodules"],"Part of the CREST pattern of limited systemic sclerosis.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Calcinosis"],
    ["#E74C3C","Red, swollen, tender breast in a breastfeeding mum with a fever","Lactational mastitis",["Breast cancer","Blocked duct only","Shingles"],"Keep feeding or expressing from that side. Antibiotics if it isn’t settling within a day.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Lactational%20mastitis"],
    ["#CB4335","A red, hot, swollen eyelid with pain on moving the eye and double vision","Orbital cellulitis",["Preseptal cellulitis","Stye","Thyroid eye disease"],"Pain on eye movement and double vision mean the infection is behind the eye. Urgent IV antibiotics and CT.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Orbital%20cellulitis"],
    ["#D9534F","Red, raw nappy area that spares the skin creases","Irritant nappy dermatitis",["Candida nappy rash","Psoriasis","Eczema"],"Urine and poo irritate the exposed skin. Candida loves the creases instead.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Irritant%20nappy%20dermatitis"],
    ["#FF6F61","Red streaks of blood mixed into stool and diarrhoea for 6 weeks in a 25-year-old","Inflammatory bowel disease",["Haemorrhoids","Infective colitis","Irritable bowel syndrome"],"Bloody diarrhoea for weeks needs stool tests, faecal calprotectin and a colonoscopy.","/inflammatory-bowel-disease/"],
    ["#EC7063","A red, smooth patch on the cervix that bleeds after sex, in someone on the pill","Cervical ectropion",["Cervical cancer","Cervicitis","Cervical polyp"],"Common and harmless with hormones, but check cervical screening is up to date.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Cervical%20ectropion"],
    ["#E35D5B","Red, itchy, ring-shaped patches on the face of a dairy farmer","Zoophilic tinea",["Eczema","Psoriasis","Lupus"],"Cattle ringworm. Animal fungi cause angrier rashes. Often needs oral antifungals.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Zoophilic%20tinea"],
    ["#F4D03F","Greasy yellow scale in the eyebrows, sides of the nose and behind the ears","Seborrhoeic dermatitis",["Psoriasis","Rosacea","Eczema"],"A reaction to Malassezia yeast. Antifungal shampoos and creams help.","/seb-derm/"],
    ["#F7DC6F","Yellow pus pointing in a red, painful lump on the eyelid edge","Stye",["Chalazion","Cellulitis","Basal cell carcinoma"],"Hordeolum. Warm compresses usually work. A painless, firm lump is a chalazion instead.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Stye"],
    ["#D4AC0D","Yellow-green, smelly discharge from one nostril in a toddler","Nasal foreign body",["Bacterial sinusitis","Adenoiditis","Choanal atresia"],"One-sided, smelly discharge in a small child: look for a bead or a bean.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Nasal%20foreign%20body"],
    ["#C9A227","Yellow, waxy, umbilicated papules on a child’s trunk","Molluscum contagiosum",["Chickenpox","Viral warts","Milia"],"A pox virus. Harmless and clears within months to a couple of years.","/molluscum/"],
    ["#239B56","Green, slimy stools in a 2-year-old who drinks lots of juice and is otherwise well","Toddler diarrhoea",["Coeliac disease","Giardiasis","Lactose intolerance"],"Common and harmless. Cut back on juice and add some fat to the diet.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Toddler%20diarrhoea"],
    ["#C0392B","Red, warm, swollen knee in a carpet layer who kneels all day","Prepatellar bursitis",["Septic arthritis","Gout","Meniscal tear"],"Housemaid’s knee. Fluid in the bursa in front of the kneecap. Aspirate if infection is possible.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Prepatellar%20bursitis"],
    ["#E74C3C","A red, swollen elbow tip after leaning on a desk for weeks","Olecranon bursitis",["Gout of the elbow","Fracture","Tennis elbow"],"Usually from pressure. Fever and redness spreading suggest infection.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Olecranon%20bursitis"],
    ["#D9534F","Red, swollen gums that bleed easily in the second trimester","Pregnancy gingivitis",["Scurvy","Leukaemia","Low platelets"],"Hormones make gums more sensitive. Good brushing and a dental check help.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pregnancy%20gingivitis"],
    ["#CB4335","Red, hot, painful lump near the anus with fever","Perianal abscess",["Haemorrhoid","Anal fissure","Pilonidal sinus"],"Needs drainage; antibiotics alone don’t cure it.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Perianal%20abscess"],
    ["#B03A2E","A red, scaly, slow-growing patch on the leg of an older woman that won’t heal","Bowen’s disease",["Eczema","Psoriasis","Tinea"],"Bowen’s disease. A non-healing scaly patch on sun-damaged skin needs a biopsy.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Bowens%20disease"],
    ["#E6564B","Red, sore eyelid edges with crusts on the lashes every morning","Blepharitis",["Conjunctivitis","Stye","Seborrhoeic dermatitis"],"Common and chronic. Daily lid hygiene with warm compresses helps.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Blepharitis"],
    ["#EC7063","A red, painful finger nail fold with pus after nail biting","Acute paronychia",["Herpetic whitlow","Felon","Gout"],"Warm soaks and drainage if there’s pus. Antibiotics only if it’s spreading.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Acute%20paronychia"],
    ["#F1948A","Red, burning, clustered blisters on a fingertip of a dental nurse","Herpetic whitlow",["Paronychia","Bullous impetigo","Felon"],"Herpes simplex. Don’t cut it open; antivirals if early.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Herpetic%20whitlow"],
    ["#F4D03F","Yellow skin and eyes, dark urine and itch, two weeks into a course of antibiotics for cellulitis","Drug-induced cholestasis",["Hepatitis A","Gallstones","Gilbert syndrome"],"Flucloxacillin can cause cholestatic liver injury, sometimes weeks after the course.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Drug-induced%20cholestasis"],
    ["#F9E79F","Yellow-white specks in an ear canal with itch and fluffy debris","Otomycosis",["Earwax","Bacterial otitis externa","Cholesteatoma"],"Fungal ear infection. Often after antibiotic ear drops. Cleaning plus antifungal drops.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Otomycosis"],
    ["#D4AC0D","A yellow-white pearly mass behind the eardrum and a smelly discharge","Cholesteatoma",["Ear infection","Earwax","Glue ear"],"Skin growing in the middle ear can erode bone. Needs ENT surgery.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Cholesteatoma"],
    ["#F5B041","Pale lemon-yellow skin, a smooth red tongue and tingling feet in a 60-year-old","Pernicious anaemia",["Jaundice from gallstones","Carotenaemia","Hypothyroidism"],"Lemon-yellow tint. Pallor plus mild jaundice from red cells breaking down in the marrow.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pernicious%20anaemia"],
    ["#52BE80","A green-blue swollen leg after a long-haul flight, now pale and cold","Arterial embolism",["DVT","Cellulitis","Lymphoedema"],"Pale, cold, pulseless and painful: an emergency. Act within hours.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Arterial%20embolism"],
    ["#2E86DE","Bluish swelling of a woman’s inner lip that feels like a soft blister","Mucocele",["Melanoma","Venous lake","Cold sore"],"A blocked minor salivary gland. Often bursts and returns; can be removed.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Mucocele"],
    ["#3867D6","A soft, dark blue papule on the lower lip of an older man that empties when pressed","Venous lake",["Melanoma","Mucocele","Kaposi sarcoma"],"A dilated vein from sun damage. Harmless; blanching on pressure is the clue.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Venous%20lake"],
    ["#8E44AD","A painful purple lump on the palm of a child with a heart murmur and fever","Osler node",["Janeway lesion","Glomus tumour","Splinter haemorrhage"],"Infective endocarditis. Painful, tender nodules from immune complexes. Blood cultures and echo.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Osler%20node"],
    ["#9B59B6","Purple-red patches on the palms that don’t hurt, in someone with fever and a new murmur","Janeway lesions",["Palmar erythema","Hand, foot and mouth","Eczema"],"Infective endocarditis. Painless septic emboli. Osler nodes are the painful ones.","/signs/janeway-lesions/"],
    ["#A569BD","Purple, swollen tongue and lips after starting a blood pressure medicine","ACE inhibitor angioedema",["Anaphylaxis","Hereditary angioedema","Food allergy"],"Bradykinin, not histamine: adrenaline and antihistamines often don’t help. Stop the ACE inhibitor for good.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=ACE%20inhibitor%20angioedema"],
    ["#FFB6C1","Pink, crusted nodule growing fast on the sun-damaged hand of an older man","Keratoacanthoma",["Squamous cell carcinoma","Basal cell carcinoma","Viral wart"],"Grows over weeks with a crater. Treated as a squamous cell cancer; remove it.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Keratoacanthoma"],
    ["#8B5A2B","Brown patches in the mouth and on the lips of a teenager with tummy pains","Peutz–Jeghers syndrome",["Addison’s disease","Laugier–Hunziker syndrome","McCune–Albright syndrome"],"Pigmented lips plus bowel polyps. Raises bowel and other cancer risks; needs surveillance.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Peutz%E2%80%93Jeghers%20syndrome"],
    ["#A0522D","Brown, fluid-filled bump at the base of the spine with a hairy dimple","Pilonidal sinus",["Boil","Spina bifida","Haemorrhoid"],"Hair works into the skin of the natal cleft. Drain abscesses; surgery for recurrent ones.","/pilonidal-sinus/"],
    ["#2C3E50","A black scab on the arm after handling sheep, ringed by swelling, painless","Cutaneous anthrax",["White-tailed spider bite","Scrub typhus","Orf"],"Rare in Australia but occurs in livestock workers. Painless black eschar with big swelling. Notifiable.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Cutaneous%20anthrax"],
    ["#17202A","Black, formed stools and a normal blood count, a week after starting a supplement for heavy periods","Iron tablets",["Upper GI bleed","Bismuth","Bowel cancer"],"Iron darkens stool but it isn’t sticky or tarry like melaena. Check if unsure.","/medicines/iron-tablets/"],
    ["#F8F9F9","A painless, firm, white-yellow lump in the middle of the eyelid after a stye","Chalazion",["Stye","Basal cell carcinoma","Milium"],"A blocked oil gland. Warm compresses; incision if it doesn’t settle.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Chalazion"],
    ["#ECF0F1","White, flat-topped bumps along a scratch line in a child (Koebner)","Plane warts",["Lichen planus","Molluscum","Milia"],"Flat warts spread along scratches. Usually clear by themselves.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Plane%20warts"],
    ["#F2F3F4","Pale white earlobe and nose tips after a night in the snow, now numb","Frostbite",["Raynaud’s","Chilblains","Vitiligo"],"Rewarm in warm (not hot) water. Don’t rub; don’t rewarm if refreezing is likely.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Frostbite"],
    ["#EAEDED","White, scaly patch in the groin with satellite spots in a person with diabetes","Candida intertrigo",["Tinea cruris","Psoriasis","Erythrasma"],"Satellite spots suggest Candida. Keep the area dry; antifungal cream.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Candida%20intertrigo"],
    ["#95A5A6","Grey, wrinkled fingertips after a long swim","Normal finding",["Raynaud’s phenomenon","Dehydration","Scleroderma"],"A nerve-controlled reflex, probably for grip. Absent wrinkling can be a sign of nerve damage.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Normal%20finding"],
    ["#E74C3C","Red, itchy, weeping rash on the earlobes and wrist where jewellery touches","Nickel allergy",["Eczema","Psoriasis","Tinea"],"Allergic contact dermatitis. Patch testing confirms it. Avoid nickel; coat or swap the metal.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Nickel%20allergy"],
    ["#F39C12","Orange-brown skin and dark knuckles in a vegan with numb feet","Vitamin B12 deficiency",["Addison’s disease","Haemochromatosis","Melasma"],"B12 deficiency can darken skin, especially knuckles. Strict vegans need B12 supplements.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Vitamin%20B12%20deficiency"],
    ["#27AE60","Green-stained fingernails in a dishwasher with a swollen nail fold","Pseudomonas paronychia",["Onychomycosis","Subungual melanoma","Subungual haematoma"],"Wet work damages the cuticle. Keep hands dry; treat the infection.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pseudomonas%20paronychia"],
    ["#3498DB","A blue-black flat patch on the gum next to an old silver filling","Amalgam tattoo",["Mucosal melanoma","Lead line","Physiological pigmentation"],"Silver filling particles in the gum. Harmless, but biopsy if unsure.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Amalgam%20tattoo"],
    ["#8E44AD","Purple, raised, firm lump that bled after a minor knock, on the gum of a pregnant woman","Pyogenic granuloma",["Gum cancer","Abscess","Kaposi sarcoma"],"Pregnancy epulis. A vascular overgrowth from hormones. Often shrinks after birth.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Pyogenic%20granuloma"],
    ["#FDFEFE","White plaques on the tongue and mouth that wipe off, in someone using a steroid inhaler","Oral thrush",["Leukoplakia","Lichen planus","Geographic tongue"],"Rinse and spit after each puff, or use a spacer. Antifungal treatment clears it.","/oral-thrush-babies/"],
    ["#C0392B","Red, burning feet and hands in hot weather that ease in cold water, with a high platelet count","Erythromelalgia",["Gout","Raynaud’s","Cellulitis"],"Can be linked to blood disorders like essential thrombocythaemia. Aspirin may help in that case.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Erythromelalgia"],
    ["#F4D03F","Yellow, shiny patches on the eyelids of a 30-year-old whose father had a heart attack at 45","Familial hypercholesterolaemia",["Diabetes","Hypothyroidism","Normal ageing"],"In young people, check lipids: familial hypercholesterolaemia needs early treatment and family testing.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Familial%20hypercholesterolaemia"],
    ["#2E86C1","Blue-grey nails and gums on long-term HIV treatment started in the 1990s","Zidovudine",["Cyanosis","Melanoma","Lead poisoning"],"Drug-induced nail pigmentation; harmless, but a clue to medication history.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Zidovudine"],
    ["#212121","Black, ‘walnut’-like cracked skin on the neck and back of a farmer","Sun damage",["Acanthosis nigricans","Ichthyosis","Pellagra"],"Sun damage. Thick, deeply lined skin from years of sun. A marker of high skin cancer risk.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Sun%20damage"]
