    ["#E53935","Red bullseye rash after a tick bite overseas","Lyme disease",["Ringworm","Cellulitis","Spider bite"],"Lyme disease. The expanding target rash is diagnostic in Lyme areas. Treat with doxycycline.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Lyme%20disease"],
    ["#AD1457","Red butterfly rash across the cheeks that spares the folds beside the nose","Systemic lupus erythematosus",["Rosacea","Dermatomyositis","Seborrhoeic dermatitis"],"The malar rash spares the nasolabial folds. Check ANA and other bloods.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Systemic%20lupus%20erythematosus"],
    ["#8E2420","Cola-coloured urine two weeks after a sore throat","Post-streptococcal glomerulonephritis",["Rhabdomyolysis","IgA nephropathy","Kidney stones"],"The kidneys inflame after strep. Blood pressure up, puffy face. Usually recovers.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Post-streptococcal%20glomerulonephritis"],
    ["#7B1F1F","Cola-coloured urine the day after a heavy gym session","Rhabdomyolysis",["Glomerulonephritis","Haemolytic anaemia","March haemoglobinuria"],"Muscle breakdown releases myoglobin. Check CK, push fluids, protect the kidneys.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Rhabdomyolysis"],
    ["#E57373","Bright red blood on the paper and sharp pain when passing hard stools","Anal fissure",["Bowel cancer","Haemorrhoids","Diverticulitis"],"Tearing pain plus bright blood is classic. Fibre, fluids and topical treatments. Painless bleeding in older people needs a scope.","/anal-fissure/"],
    ["#C2185B","Bright red ‘slapped cheeks’ in a child, then a lacy rash on the arms","Parvovirus B19",["Scarlet fever","Measles","Rubella"],"Parvovirus B19. Usually mild, but can cause problems in pregnancy and in people with blood disorders.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Search?search=Parvovirus%20B19"],
    ["#880E4F","Which colour change in a feverish child needs an ambulance now?","A purple rash that doesn’t fade under a glass",["Orange urine on a new antibiotic","Green snot with a cold","Red cheeks after crying"],"A fever with a spreading rash that doesn’t fade under a glass is meningococcal sepsis until proven otherwise.","/meningococcal/"]
